I walk to the counter.
There is a big menu there.
I look at the menu.
A worker is standing at the counter.
He looks at me and smiles.
"Namaskaram," he says.
"What do you want?" he asks.
"Namaskaram," I say.
I am very thirsty.
I want a cold drink.
"Can I get a big glass of iced tea?" I ask.
"Yes, you can get it," he says.
I am also slightly hungry.
I look at the menu again.
"Can you give me a piece of banana cake?" I ask.
"I can certainly give it," he says.
"Do you want anything else?" he asks.
"No, just this is enough," I say.
"Thank you very much."
I go back to my table.
